    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, from the HTTP boundary through persistence.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Security (before the method runs)\n1. **Authentication** \u2014 When `petclinic.security.enable=true`, HTTP Basic auth is required (`anyRequest().authenticated()`).\n2. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `addOwner` requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`; failure \u2192 403. (When security is disabled, neither is enforced.)\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on the request body\nTriggered by `@Validated` + `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`. Any failure \u2192 `400` via `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`. Constraints:\n3. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`\n4. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")`\n5. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")` (non-blank)\n6. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n7. `address` (optional) \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`\n8. `addressLine1` (optional) \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`\n9. `addressLine2` (optional) \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n10. `email` (optional) \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n11. `postcode` (optional) \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n12. `registrationDate` / `birthDate` (optional) \u2014 `@Valid` LocalDate\n- (`title`, `sharesHousehold` have no constraints.)\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 `OwnerRegistrar.register(...)` business pipeline (in order)\nFailures here return bare status codes (`400/409/429`), bypassing the advice.\n\n13. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header; if a prior create with that key still exists, returns that owner with **`200 OK`** and stops (no new create). Backed by an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap` on the singleton.\n14. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (MapStruct; `id` and `pets` ignored).\n15. **Default registrationDate** \u2014 null \u2192 `LocalDate.now()`. *(side-effect: sets field)*\n16. **Reject future registrationDate** \u2192 `400`.\n17. **Roll forward to a business day** \u2014 advances past weekends and fixed 2026 holidays. *(side-effect: mutates registrationDate)*\n18. **Per-day quota** \u2014 \u2265 100 owners on that registrationDate \u2192 `429`.\n19. **Address normalization** \u2014 prefers `addressLine1/2` over flat `address`, normalizes; no usable address \u2192 `400`. *(side-effect: mutates address fields)*\n20. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 E.164 normalize; null \u2192 `400`; then national-number length check \u2192 `400`. *(side-effect: stores canonical form)*\n21. **Email validation** \u2014 trim; regex check \u2192 `400`; reject disposable domains (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 `400`. *(side-effect: stores lower-cased)*\n22. **Postcode validation** \u2014 `^[0-9]{4}$` **and** valid for the city's region (`CityRegionResolver`) \u2192 else `400`.\n23. **Assign household id** \u2014 SHA-256 prefix of normalized lastName + postcode. *(side-effect: sets field)*\n24. **Household duplicate rule** \u2014 existing owner shares household id and `sharesHousehold` \u2260 true \u2192 `409`.\n25. **Hard duplicate rule** \u2014 any non-deleted owner with same identityKey (`telephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 `409`.\n26. **Per-city quota** \u2014 \u2265 50 owners in the normalized city \u2192 `409`.\n27. **Derived-field enrichment** \u2014 sets `customerCode` (region + de-duplicated hash), `namesakeCount`, `membershipNumber`, `bulkSignupWarning` (>80/day), and soft-match `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. *(side-effects: multiple fields set)*\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Persistence & post-actions\n28. **Save** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(...)`, in its own `@Transactional` (the registrar itself is not transactional, so all the prior reads and this save are separate transactions). `CallMonitoringAspect` wraps the repository call for JMX metrics. `Owner.pets` cascade `ALL` exists but is a no-op here (empty collection).\n29. **Record idempotency key** \u2014 stores key \u2192 new owner id in the in-memory map. *(side-effect)*\n30. **Audit log** \u2014 INFO line to the dedicated `\"AUDIT\"` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber). This is the only notification-type side-effect \u2014 **no email sent, no application events published**.\n31. **Response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **`201 CREATED`**.\n\n## Notes\n- The `Owner` **entity** carries its own constraints (`@NotEmpty` address/city, `@Pattern` telephone `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, `@Email`), but nothing runs a validator on the entity in this flow (no `@PrePersist`/`@EntityListeners`), so those are **not enforced** on create.\n- No `@InitBinder`, no custom constraint on this path (the `PetAgeValidator` is Pets-only), no `ApplicationListener`/`@EventListener`, no password encoding (owners have no password).\n\nNothing was modified."
